IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cb2-nouns`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), Part X, section 120 -- DISCLOSURE OF A DIRECTOR'S OR
-- OFFICER'S INTEREST IN A MATERIAL CONTRACT OR TRANSACTION. Layer 1.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Encoded from a plain-text rendering of the Justice Canada consolidation current to
-- 2026-09-30, which is not an official version; nothing here is verified against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RULE. Named `<what it works out> within s <section>`. Where a provision says what follows in
-- a stated case, the rule is TRUE when that case holds; FALSE means only that this provision does not apply.
-- A rule whose result is a MAYBE returns NOTHING where the text is silent for the case.
-- Within this module a rule that depends on a sibling calls it and takes its inputs. A cross-reference to
-- another piece is a plain input and says so. Dates are whole days (fork F-P10-12).

§ `s 120 Disclosure of interest`

§§ `s 120(1) Disclosure of interest`

-- src:1438 | Disclosure of interest
-- src:1439 | 120 (1) A director or an officer of a corporation shall disclose to the corporation, in writing or by requesting to have it entered in the minutes of meetings of directors or of meetings of committees of directors, the nature and extent of any interest that he or she has in a material contract or material transaction, whether made or proposed, with the corporation, if the director or officer
-- src:1440 | (a) is a party to the contract or transaction;
-- src:1441 | (b) is a director or an officer, or an individual acting in a similar capacity, of a party to the contract or transaction; or
-- src:1442 | (c) has a material interest in a party to the contract or transaction.
@ref CBCA s 120(1) (src:1438-1442)
GIVEN `the contract or transaction is a material contract or material transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract or transaction is with the corporation, whether made or proposed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a party to the contract or transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a director or an officer, or an individual acting in a similar capacity, of a party to the contract or transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a material interest in a party to the contract or transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the director or officer must disclose the interest within s 120(1)` MEANS
        `the contract or transaction is a material contract or material transaction`
    AND `the contract or transaction is with the corporation, whether made or proposed`
    AND (   `the person is a party to the contract or transaction`
         OR `the person is a director or an officer, or an individual acting in a similar capacity, of a party to the contract or transaction`
         OR `the person has a material interest in a party to the contract or transaction`)

-- The manner: to the corporation, in writing or by requesting to have it entered in the minutes of meetings of
-- directors or of meetings of committees of directors, stating the nature and extent of the interest.
-- src:1438 | Disclosure of interest
-- src:1439 | 120 (1) A director or an officer of a corporation shall disclose to the corporation, in writing or by requesting to have it entered in the minutes of meetings of directors or of meetings of committees of directors, the nature and extent of any interest that he or she has in a material contract or material transaction, whether made or proposed, with the corporation, if the director or officer
@ref CBCA s 120(1) (src:1438-1439)
GIVEN `the disclosure is made to the corporation in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is made by requesting to have it entered in the minutes of meetings of directors or of committees of directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure states the nature and extent of the interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the disclosure is made in the manner required within s 120(1)` MEANS
        (   `the disclosure is made to the corporation in writing`
         OR `the disclosure is made by requesting to have it entered in the minutes of meetings of directors or of committees of directors`)
    AND `the disclosure states the nature and extent of the interest`

§§ `s 120(2) Time of disclosure for director`

-- The latest meeting at which the director must disclose: (a) the meeting at which a proposed contract or
-- transaction is first considered; (b), (c) and (d) the first meeting after the director becomes interested, or
-- becomes a director. Where more than one paragraph applies, the earliest governs, since a disclosure made then
-- covers the later ones. A meeting held on the day of the event counts as after it (fork F-P10-12). NOTHING: no
-- paragraph applies yet, or no meeting has been held since.
-- src:1443 | Time of disclosure for director
-- src:1444 | (2) The disclosure required by subsection (1) shall be made, in the case of a director,
-- src:1445 | (a) at the meeting at which a proposed contract or transaction is first considered;
-- src:1446 | (b) if the director was not, at the time of the meeting referred to in paragraph (a), interested in a proposed contract or transaction, at the first meeting after he or she becomes so interested;
-- src:1447 | (c) if the director becomes interested after a contract or transaction is made, at the first meeting after he or she becomes so interested; or
-- src:1448 | (d) if an individual who is interested in a contract or transaction later becomes a director, at the first meeting after he or she becomes a director.
@ref CBCA s 120(2) (src:1443-1448)
GIVEN `the date of the meeting at which a proposed contract or transaction is first considered, if there is one` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date the director becomes interested in a proposed contract or transaction that they were not interested in at that meeting, if they do` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date the director becomes interested after a contract or transaction is made, if they do` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date an individual who is interested in a contract or transaction later becomes a director, if they do` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the dates on which meetings of directors are held` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the latest meeting at which the director must disclose within s 120(2)` MEANS
    `the earlier of`
        `the date of the meeting at which a proposed contract or transaction is first considered, if there is one`
        (`the earlier of`
            (`the first meeting after` `the date the director becomes interested in a proposed contract or transaction that they were not interested in at that meeting, if they do`)
            (`the earlier of`
                (`the first meeting after` `the date the director becomes interested after a contract or transaction is made, if they do`)
                (`the first meeting after` `the date an individual who is interested in a contract or transaction later becomes a director, if they do`)))
    WHERE
        `the earlier of` a b MEANS
            CONSIDER a
            WHEN NOTHING THEN b
            WHEN JUST x THEN
                CONSIDER b
                WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST x
                WHEN JUST y THEN JUST (IF x LESS THAN y THEN x ELSE y)
        `the first meeting on or after` event dates MEANS
            CONSIDER dates
            WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
            WHEN d FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
                IF d AT LEAST event
                THEN `the earlier of` (JUST d) (`the first meeting on or after` event rest)
                ELSE `the first meeting on or after` event rest
        `the first meeting after` maybeEvent MEANS
            CONSIDER maybeEvent
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST event THEN `the first meeting on or after` event `the dates on which meetings of directors are held`

§§ `s 120(3) Time of disclosure for officer`

-- An officer who is not a director: "immediately after" the first of (a) becoming aware that the contract,
-- transaction, proposed contract or proposed transaction is to be considered or has been considered at a
-- meeting, (b) becoming interested after a contract or transaction is made, (c) becoming an officer while
-- interested in a contract. "Immediately after" is read as the same day (fork F-P10-13). NOTHING: none has
-- happened yet.
-- src:1449 | Time of disclosure for officer
-- src:1450 | (3) The disclosure required by subsection (1) shall be made, in the case of an officer who is not a director,
-- src:1451 | (a) immediately after he or she becomes aware that the contract, transaction, proposed contract or proposed transaction is to be considered or has been considered at a meeting;
-- src:1452 | (b) if the officer becomes interested after a contract or transaction is made, immediately after he or she becomes so interested; or
-- src:1453 | (c) if an individual who is interested in a contract later becomes an officer, immediately after he or she becomes an officer.
@ref CBCA s 120(3) (src:1449-1453)
GIVEN `the date the officer becomes aware that the contract or transaction is to be considered or has been considered at a meeting, if they do` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date the officer becomes interested after a contract or transaction is made, if they do` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date an individual who is interested in a contract later becomes an officer, if they do` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the last day for the officer to disclose within s 120(3)` MEANS
    `the earlier of`
        `the date the officer becomes aware that the contract or transaction is to be considered or has been considered at a meeting, if they do`
        (`the earlier of`
            `the date the officer becomes interested after a contract or transaction is made, if they do`
            `the date an individual who is interested in a contract later becomes an officer, if they do`)
    WHERE
        `the earlier of` a b MEANS
            CONSIDER a
            WHEN NOTHING THEN b
            WHEN JUST x THEN
                CONSIDER b
                WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST x
                WHEN JUST y THEN JUST (IF x LESS THAN y THEN x ELSE y)

§§ `s 120(4) Time of disclosure for director or officer`

-- NOTHING: the contract or transaction is one that, in the ordinary course of the corporation's business, would
-- require approval by the directors or shareholders, so s 120(4) says nothing and (2) and (3) govern.
-- src:1454 | Time of disclosure for director or officer
-- src:1455 | (4) If a material contract or material transaction, whether entered into or proposed, is one that, in the ordinary course of the corporation’s business, would not require approval by the directors or shareholders, a director or officer shall disclose, in writing to the corporation or request to have it entered in the minutes of meetings of directors or of meetings of committees of directors, the nature and extent of his or her interest immediately after he or she becomes aware of the contract or transaction.
@ref CBCA s 120(4) (src:1454-1455)
GIVEN `the contract or transaction is one that, in the ordinary course of the corporation's business, would not require approval by the directors or shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the director or officer becomes aware of the contract or transaction` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the last day for the director or officer to disclose within s 120(4)` MEANS
    IF `the contract or transaction is one that, in the ordinary course of the corporation's business, would not require approval by the directors or shareholders`
    THEN JUST `the date the director or officer becomes aware of the contract or transaction`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Whether a disclosure made on a day is late: it is not late if it is made no later than the last day. A
-- disclosure made earlier than the meeting is read as not late (fork F-P10-12). With no last day (NOTHING above)
-- nothing is yet due, so it is not late.
-- src:1443 | Time of disclosure for director
-- src:1444 | (2) The disclosure required by subsection (1) shall be made, in the case of a director,
-- src:1445 | (a) at the meeting at which a proposed contract or transaction is first considered;
-- src:1446 | (b) if the director was not, at the time of the meeting referred to in paragraph (a), interested in a proposed contract or transaction, at the first meeting after he or she becomes so interested;
-- src:1447 | (c) if the director becomes interested after a contract or transaction is made, at the first meeting after he or she becomes so interested; or
-- src:1448 | (d) if an individual who is interested in a contract or transaction later becomes a director, at the first meeting after he or she becomes a director.
-- src:1449 | Time of disclosure for officer
-- src:1450 | (3) The disclosure required by subsection (1) shall be made, in the case of an officer who is not a director,
-- src:1451 | (a) immediately after he or she becomes aware that the contract, transaction, proposed contract or proposed transaction is to be considered or has been considered at a meeting;
-- src:1452 | (b) if the officer becomes interested after a contract or transaction is made, immediately after he or she becomes so interested; or
-- src:1453 | (c) if an individual who is interested in a contract later becomes an officer, immediately after he or she becomes an officer.
-- src:1454 | Time of disclosure for director or officer
-- src:1455 | (4) If a material contract or material transaction, whether entered into or proposed, is one that, in the ordinary course of the corporation’s business, would not require approval by the directors or shareholders, a director or officer shall disclose, in writing to the corporation or request to have it entered in the minutes of meetings of directors or of meetings of committees of directors, the nature and extent of his or her interest immediately after he or she becomes aware of the contract or transaction.
@ref CBCA s 120(2) s 120(3) s 120(4) (src:1443-1455)
GIVEN `the last day for the disclosure under subsection 120(2), (3) or (4), if there is one` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date the disclosure is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the disclosure is not late within s 120(2) to (4)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the last day for the disclosure under subsection 120(2), (3) or (4), if there is one`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST last THEN `the date the disclosure is made` AT MOST last

§§ `s 120(5) Voting`

-- "A director required to make a disclosure under subsection (1)" is worked out by `the director or officer must
-- disclose the interest within s 120(1)`, called here.
-- src:1456 | Voting
-- src:1457 | (5) A director required to make a disclosure under subsection (1) shall not vote on any resolution to approve the contract or transaction unless the contract or transaction
-- src:1458 | (a) relates primarily to his or her remuneration as a director, officer, employee, agent or mandatary of the corporation or an affiliate;
-- src:1459 | (b) is for indemnity or insurance under section 124; or
-- src:1460 | (c) is with an affiliate.
@ref CBCA s 120(5) (src:1456-1460)
GIVEN `the contract or transaction is a material contract or material transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract or transaction is with the corporation, whether made or proposed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a party to the contract or transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a director or an officer, or an individual acting in a similar capacity, of a party to the contract or transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a material interest in a party to the contract or transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract or transaction relates primarily to the director's remuneration as a director, officer, employee, agent or mandatary of the corporation or an affiliate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract or transaction is for indemnity or insurance under section 124` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract or transaction is with an affiliate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the director shall not vote on the resolution to approve the contract or transaction within s 120(5)` MEANS
        `the director or officer must disclose the interest within s 120(1)`
            `the contract or transaction is a material contract or material transaction`
            `the contract or transaction is with the corporation, whether made or proposed`
            `the person is a party to the contract or transaction`
            `the person is a director or an officer, or an individual acting in a similar capacity, of a party to the contract or transaction`
            `the person has a material interest in a party to the contract or transaction`
    AND (NOT (   `the contract or transaction relates primarily to the director's remuneration as a director, officer, employee, agent or mandatary of the corporation or an affiliate`
              OR `the contract or transaction is for indemnity or insurance under section 124`
              OR `the contract or transaction is with an affiliate`))

§§ `s 120(6) Continuing disclosure`

-- src:1461 | Continuing disclosure
-- src:1462 | (6) For the purposes of this section, a general notice to the directors declaring that a director or an officer is to be regarded as interested, for any of the following reasons, in a contract or transaction made with a party, is a sufficient declaration of interest in relation to the contract or transaction:
-- src:1463 | (a) the director or officer is a director or officer, or acting in a similar capacity, of a party referred to in paragraph (1)(b) or (c);
-- src:1464 | (b) the director or officer has a material interest in the party; or
-- src:1465 | (c) there has been a material change in the nature of the director’s or the officer’s interest in the party.
@ref CBCA s 120(6) (src:1461-1465)
GIVEN `a general notice is given to the directors declaring that the director or officer is to be regarded as interested` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract or transaction is made with the party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director or officer is a director or officer, or acting in a similar capacity, of a party referred to in paragraph 120(1)(b) or (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director or officer has a material interest in the party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there has been a material change in the nature of the director's or the officer's interest in the party` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the general notice is a sufficient declaration of interest within s 120(6)` MEANS
        `a general notice is given to the directors declaring that the director or officer is to be regarded as interested`
    AND `the contract or transaction is made with the party`
    AND (   `the director or officer is a director or officer, or acting in a similar capacity, of a party referred to in paragraph 120(1)(b) or (c)`
         OR `the director or officer has a material interest in the party`
         OR `there has been a material change in the nature of the director's or the officer's interest in the party`)

§§ `s 120(6.1) Access to disclosures`

-- src:1466 | Access to disclosures
-- src:1467 | (6.1) The shareholders of the corporation may examine the portions of any minutes of meetings of directors or of committees of directors that contain disclosures under this section, and any other documents that contain those disclosures, during the usual business hours of the corporation.
@ref CBCA s 120(6.1) (src:1466-1467)
GIVEN `the person is a shareholder of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the portion of the minutes, or the other document, contains disclosures under section 120` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the examination is during the usual business hours of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the shareholder may examine the minutes or document within s 120(6.1)` MEANS
        `the person is a shareholder of the corporation`
    AND `the portion of the minutes, or the other document, contains disclosures under section 120`
    AND `the examination is during the usual business hours of the corporation`

§§ `s 120(7) Avoidance standards`

-- "Disclosure of the interest was made in accordance with subsections (1) to (6)" is a plain input: the rules of
-- this section work it out, and the caller says whether they were met.
-- src:1468 | Avoidance standards
-- src:1469 | (7) A contract or transaction for which disclosure is required under subsection (1) is not invalid, and the director or officer is not accountable to the corporation or its shareholders for any profit realized from the contract or transaction, because of the director’s or officer’s interest in the contract or transaction or because the director was present or was counted to determine whether a quorum existed at the meeting of directors or committee of directors that considered the contract or transaction, if
-- src:1470 | (a) disclosure of the interest was made in accordance with subsections (1) to (6);
-- src:1471 | (b) the directors approved the contract or transaction; and
-- src:1472 | (c) the contract or transaction was reasonable and fair to the corporation when it was approved.
@ref CBCA s 120(7) (src:1468-1472)
GIVEN `the ground is the director's or officer's interest, or that the director was present or was counted to determine whether a quorum existed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `disclosure of the interest was made in accordance with subsections 120(1) to (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors approved the contract or transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract or transaction was reasonable and fair to the corporation when it was approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the contract is not invalid and the director or officer is not accountable for the profit within s 120(7)` MEANS
        `the ground is the director's or officer's interest, or that the director was present or was counted to determine whether a quorum existed`
    AND `disclosure of the interest was made in accordance with subsections 120(1) to (6)`
    AND `the directors approved the contract or transaction`
    AND `the contract or transaction was reasonable and fair to the corporation when it was approved`

§§ `s 120(7.1) Confirmation by shareholders`

-- src:1473 | Confirmation by shareholders
-- src:1474 | (7.1) Even if the conditions of subsection (7) are not met, a director or officer, acting honestly and in good faith, is not accountable to the corporation or to its shareholders for any profit realized from a contract or transaction for which disclosure is required under subsection (1), and the contract or transaction is not invalid by reason only of the interest of the director or officer in the contract or transaction, if
-- src:1475 | (a) the contract or transaction is approved or confirmed by special resolution at a meeting of the shareholders;
-- src:1476 | (b) disclosure of the interest was made to the shareholders in a manner sufficient to indicate its nature before the contract or transaction was approved or confirmed; and
-- src:1477 | (c) the contract or transaction was reasonable and fair to the corporation when it was approved or confirmed.
@ref CBCA s 120(7.1) (src:1473-1477)
GIVEN `the director or officer acted honestly and in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract or transaction is approved or confirmed by special resolution at a meeting of the shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `disclosure of the interest was made to the shareholders in a manner sufficient to indicate its nature before the contract or transaction was approved or confirmed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract or transaction was reasonable and fair to the corporation when it was approved or confirmed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the contract is not invalid and the director or officer is not accountable for the profit even if subsection 120(7) is not met within s 120(7.1)` MEANS
        `the director or officer acted honestly and in good faith`
    AND `the contract or transaction is approved or confirmed by special resolution at a meeting of the shareholders`
    AND `disclosure of the interest was made to the shareholders in a manner sufficient to indicate its nature before the contract or transaction was approved or confirmed`
    AND `the contract or transaction was reasonable and fair to the corporation when it was approved or confirmed`

§§ `s 120(8) Application to court`

DECLARE `Order a court may make under s 120(8)` IS ONE OF
    `set aside the contract or transaction on any terms that the court thinks fit`
    `require the director or officer to account to the corporation for any profit or gain realized on it`

-- "Or do both those things": the court may make either order, or both.
-- src:1478 | Application to court
-- src:1479 | (8) If a director or an officer of a corporation fails to comply with this section, a court may, on application of the corporation or any of its shareholders, set aside the contract or transaction on any terms that it thinks fit, or require the director or officer to account to the corporation for any profit or gain realized on it, or do both those things.
@ref CBCA s 120(8) (src:1478-1479)
GIVEN `the director or officer fails to comply with section 120` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant is the corporation or one of its shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `Order a court may make under s 120(8)`
`the orders the court may make within s 120(8)` MEANS
    IF `the director or officer fails to comply with section 120` AND `the applicant is the corporation or one of its shareholders`
    THEN LIST `set aside the contract or transaction on any terms that the court thinks fit`,
              `require the director or officer to account to the corporation for any profit or gain realized on it`
    ELSE EMPTY
